# These are executed by Linux CI runners. A CRLF here is not cosmetic: it breaks shell
# heredoc terminators (a line reading "SQL\r" never matches the "SQL" delimiter) and
# trails an invisible \r onto every variable a script assigns. Windows checkouts get LF
# for these files regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
